<section class="w2-faq" id="faq" aria-labelledby="w2-faq-title">
  <div class="w2-faq-grid">
    <div class="w2-faq-heading"><p class="w2-kicker"><b>08</b> Answers before you call</p><h2 class="w2-heading" id="w2-faq-title">A few things <em>worth knowing.</em></h2><p class="w2-intro">Every property is different. These answers help you understand the inspection conversation.</p><a class="w2-faq-cta" href="#contact">Still have a question? <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    <div class="w2-faq-list">
      <details><summary>What are common signs of a hidden water leak?<i aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><p>Possible clues include a higher water bill without a clear cause, damp or discolored surfaces, a persistent musty smell, warm flooring, or water sounds when fixtures are off. These can have other causes too, so an inspection is needed to confirm a leak.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Will you have to cut into my wall or floor?<i aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><p>Leak detection can often begin with visual checks and specialized tests. The inspection is intended to locate and document the likely source; opening walls, floors, or concrete is not part of the detection visit.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What methods can help locate the leak?<i aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><p>Depending on the plumbing and symptoms, a technician may use acoustic listening, thermal imaging, pressure testing, or other methods. Ask which tests are appropriate for your situation.</p></details>
      <details><summary>How long does a leak detection visit take?<i aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><p>Timing varies with the size of the property, access to plumbing, and how many lines or areas need checking. Share what you’ve noticed when you request an appointment for a more useful estimate.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can a technician check a leak under a slab or in the yard?<i aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><p>Some leak detection providers inspect slab, under-floor, and buried water lines. Confirm which line types and locations the provider covers before booking.</p></details>
      <details><summary>How much does leak detection cost?<i aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><p>Cost depends on the property and diagnostic work involved. Ask about the visit fee and exactly which inspection methods and findings it includes before you schedule. This service covers leak detection only.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do you serve my part of Houston?<i aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><p>Service boundaries differ by provider and can change. Share your ZIP code or address area to confirm current availability.</p></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
